{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261112T032040Z-3cab7552", "ts": "2026-11-12T03:23:56Z", "actor": {"worktree": "pool-only", "plugin": "3.8.1-dev", "branch": "chore/pool-only"}, "body": {"base_commit": "c53d2927519822da2c93157a592abf978f04227e", "base_tree": "c46f0f0fdc625ef040d6bbdd6ec9367c873c3abd", "head_tree": "b54fdcdb462c98e8fda599e999462ec0ffce3810", "head_commit": null, "dispatch_commit": "c53d2927519822da2c93157a592abf978f04227e", "mode": "chunk (lighter pass, not ready for push)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit: chunk (requested by caller)", "stage": "inner", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["CHANGELOG.md", "CLAUDE.md", "docs/testing.md", "scripts/check-all.sh", "scripts/ci-unit-tests.sh", "scripts/test.sh", "tests/enforcement/test_ci_unit_shards.py", "tests/test_check_all_script.py", "tests/test_ci_unit_tests_script.py", "tests/test_test_sh_script.py"], "files_changed": ["CHANGELOG.md", "CLAUDE.md", "docs/testing.md", "scripts/check-all.sh", "scripts/ci-unit-tests.sh", "scripts/test.sh", "tests/enforcement/test_ci_unit_shards.py", "tests/test_check_all_script.py", "tests/test_ci_unit_tests_script.py", "tests/test_test_sh_script.py"], "files_oracle": [], "findings": [], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "The runbook's 'On another machine' path leads a no-testament machine into the one-session whole-suite run the same runbook forbids", "recommendation": "instance. The owner's fallback is 'go to another machine and run locally there'. docs/testing.md tells that machine 'With no testament installed, test.sh runs locally, as it always has', and 'Before a PR' says to run check-all.sh. On a machine with no testament, check-all.sh -> test.sh runs `uv run pytest packages/ tests/ -n 4` as one session. That is the same run the runbook forbids four paragraphs earlier ('Never TESTAMENT=off ./scripts/check-all.sh ... OOM-killed four workers on 16 GB'), and no guard stops it. README's Contributing step 3 sends external contributors down the same path. Add one line to 'On another machine': check-all there runs the unit suite in one session, so on 16 GB or less run `TESTAMENT_OFF_REASON=... ./scripts/ci-unit-tests.sh` for the unit suite instead.", "files": ["docs/testing.md"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "check-all reads every test.sh exit 2 as 'testament gave no verdict', and the runbook calls that line expected", "recommendation": "instance. scripts/check-all.sh:22-24 continues on any status 2. Some exit-2 sources are not a pool outage: test.sh's own refusal (TESTAMENT=off with no reason, test.sh:190); testament's `path_not_found` and `population_mismatch`; and `batches_lost` when pytest itself died in a batch, which can be the code's fault. With an env gate such as RECORD set, the local route also passes pytest's own 2 (a collection error) straight through under set -e (test.sh:250). In each case the closing line says 'Every other check passed', and the runbook says 'That line is expected'. The gate still exits non-zero, and on a live pool CI's shards would catch it, so this is a misleading label, not a false green. The cheapest fix is runbook prose: the line is expected only when testament's error code above it is one of the pool or machine codes listed under 'How it shows'. Alternatively, have check-all name test.sh's last error line.", "files": ["scripts/check-all.sh", "docs/testing.md"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "Two runbook diagnostics name the wrong testament code or command", "recommendation": "instance. docs/testing.md 'How it shows' maps a revoked key to `machine_not_set_up`. testament 0.45.1 reports a revoked key as `unauthorized` (unknown API key) or `revoked`, and `machine_not_set_up` means no coordinator or key at all (client.py:247; `testament guide client` troubleshooting). 'On another machine' says to enrol with `testament login`. A machine that has never enrolled needs `testament login --console <console>`, or it fails with `no_console`. Add `unauthorized`/`revoked` to the machine line, and write `testament login --console <console>`. Verified as accurate: `testament run --probe` and `testament status [--json]` with `coordinator_version`, the `uv tool install --force --python 3.14 git+ssh://...@v<version>` line (it matches testament's own guide), and the TESTAMENT_CI repo variable (ci.yml:56, ci-unit-pool.sh:188).", "files": ["docs/testing.md"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Without exec, a SIGTERM sent to test.sh's pid orphans the testament client", "recommendation": "instance. test.sh now runs testament as a foreground child (test.sh:214/216) instead of exec'ing it. Ctrl-C is fine: testament's main() turns KeyboardInterrupt into 130, test.sh passes 130 through, and check-all stops because 130 is neither 0 nor 2. But a SIGTERM aimed at test.sh's pid alone (`timeout ./scripts/test.sh`, or a harness killing by pid) kills bash, which has no trap, and leaves testament running its pool request with no parent. Either accept this (process-group kills, which CI cancellation and terminals use, reach testament), or run testament in the background and add `trap 'kill -TERM \"$pid\" 2>/dev/null' TERM INT` before `wait`.", "files": ["scripts/test.sh"], "oid": "O-4"}], "duration_seconds": 600, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `chore/pool-only`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": ["CHANGELOG.md", "CLAUDE.md", "docs/testing.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-cor